Z||000000||Cheever3000||09-27-2001||08:33 PM||||I've had Nationwide auto insurance for 16 years.  Don't like the cost but haven't found anything cheaper yet (didn't look very hard tho).  What I really didn't like was when I wrecked my GT two years ago, I had to talk to <I>at least</I> seven different people before it was completely resolved.  That shouldn't happen; you should only have to talk to your agent, and they take care of everything and keep you informed!<P>But I digress.  For my 94 minivan (106,000 miles) and 88GT (66,000) my wife & I are paying $754 every 6 months.  I called to ask what it would cost to add my 16 year old son driving my 88 Coupe which is not currently insured.  They said it would cost an additional $750 every 6 months (good thing I was sitting down), with only the legally required coverage.  If he could get a 3.0 GPA or better, that would drop the price $71.<P>You may be aware that CFOG-I is working out a group auto insurance deal, but it's not finalized yet.  I will be as interested as anybody to see what becomes of it, and will let you know.  Meanwhile, the boy will ride the school bus.  It just can't make turns like a Fiero, and can't get up to speed because of all the stops, but that's the deal until he gets a job or a friend who drives.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><BR>Vice President, <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||4
